  "notes": "{到達|とうたつ}する means to reach or arrive at a destination, goal, or level after effort or progress. More formal than {着|つ}く and emphasizes the culmination of a process.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pattern: ～に{到達|とうたつ}する\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {目標|もくひょう}に{到達|とうたつ}する: to reach a goal\n- {山頂|さんちょう}に{到達|とうたつ}する: to reach the summit\n- {到達|とうたつ}{点|てん}: point reached, attainment level\n- {到達|とうたつ}{度|ど}: degree of attainment\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {着|つ}く: to arrive (everyday, less formal)\n- {達成|たっせい}する: to achieve, to accomplish (focuses on completing a goal)\n- {達|たっ}する: to reach (slightly less formal than {到達|とうたつ})",
